after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The curl versionlock was directly exercised before and after a successful node restart, while the OS release and kernel remained unchanged. The restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, observed interruption, changed boot identity, and recovered running/package/service state; fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate it.","limitations":["The update behavior was tested with targeted `dnf upgrade curl` operations rather than a full-system upgrade. This directly tests the relevant package-selection behavior while avoiding unrelated platform changes, but it is not a literal full update transaction.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the versionlock configuration itself; persistence is instead established by direct post-restart command evidence."]}
